  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The following table shows the velocity of a plane during a $20$-minute trip.\n\n| $t\\,(\\text{minutes})$ | $0$ | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $v(t)\\,(\\text{kilometers/minute})$ | $17$ | $25$ | $27$ | $k$ | $18$ |\n\nIf the right Riemann sum approximation of the total distance traveled during this period has a value of  $450\\,\\text{km}$, what is the value of $k?$\n\n*Hint: The distance traveled is given by the area under the velocity-time graph.*",
  "worked_solution": "The area $A$ under the curve $y=v(t)$ can be approximated using the formula\n\n$$\nA\u2248(\\overset{\\text{heights}}{\\overset{\u23de}{v(5)+v(10)+v(15)+v(20)}})\\cdot {{\u0394t}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{width}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we now set up a table with the values of $v(t)$ at each point:\n\n| $t$ | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $v(t)$ | $25$ | $27$ | $k$ | $18$ |\n\nNow, we obtain the following approximation for the area:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & \u2248(25+27+k+18)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =5(k+70) \\\\  & =5k+350\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in the given context, the area under the curve represents the total distance traveled during the $20$ minute period. Since we are given that the right Riemann sum approximation of the total distance is $450\\,\\text{km},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5k+350 & =450 \\\\ 5k & =450-350 \\\\ k & =\\frac{100}{5} \\\\ k & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
